l with W3\u00d73 as a pung base and multiple flexible sequences. By staying concealed, I preserve the possibility of \"Fully Concealed Hand\" (6 points) or \"Concealed Hand\" (2 points). The T2-T3-T4-T5\u00d72 tiles give me flexibility to wait for either T2 or T5 to complete various patterns. More importantly, exposing a chow now would limit my options and reduce potential scoring patterns. With multiple tiles still unshown (W6\u00d74, B4\u00d73), I have good drawing chances.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
